.Dd October 28, 2026
.Dt VPS-DEPLOY-STATIC 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm vps-deploy-static
.Nd install the RAILS/__other static sites on the production VPS
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm all | sommerseth | alfa
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the deploy entry point for the static brand exports at
.Pa RAILS/__other :
.Sy sommerseth
serves thor.brgen.no from /var/www/sommerseth on loopback port 38191 and
.Sy alfa
serves alfa.brgen.no from /var/www/alfa on loopback port 38192, behind the
same relayd TLS termination as the Rails fleet. It is not a
.Xr vps-deploy 8
target: those deploy rcctl-managed Rails apps, and these sites are served by
httpd vhosts with no daemon to restart. The sites are plain trees of
HTML, CSS, vanilla JS, self-hosted fonts and images \(em no build step,
no package manager, no node_modules; the tree in git is the tree that
serves.
.Pp
Run it on vm23 as the unprivileged account
.Cm dev ,
not as root and not wrapped in
.Xr doas 1 ;
the script escalates only for the individual steps that require it, and root
cannot reach the git remote for the pull that should precede a deploy.
.Pp
For each target the script checks that the tree looks like a site
(index.html, assets/, images/), replaces the chroot tree wholesale with
its content files — the previous tree is removed first, because a
half-updated tree, old assets next to new HTML, is exactly the
almost-works a static site must never ship; README.md documents the tree
and is deliberately not installed — and then verifies that the loopback
vhost answers and returns the site's title. A green exit therefore means
deployed and serving on loopback, not merely copied. When nothing listens
on the loopback port the failure names the activation steps recorded at
the bottom of OPENBSD/etc/relayd.conf (certificate SANs, config install,
restart) rather than pretending the site is up.
.Pp
The accepted targets are
.Cm all ,
.Cm sommerseth ,
and
.Cm alfa .
Unknown targets are refused before anything is copied.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "REMOTE_PUB4"
.It Ev REMOTE_PUB4
Path to the pub4 checkout on the box. The default is /home/dev/pub4.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width "1"
.It 0
Every target was installed into the chroot and answered
on its loopback port with the expected title.
.It 1
At least one target failed; earlier targets that succeeded stay deployed.
.It 2
Usage error, unknown target, or an attempt to run as root.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr vps-deploy 8
